    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for libXi",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for libXi fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-93541: out-of-bounds read in XQueryDeviceState() (bsc#1281605).\n- CVE-2026-93542: out-of-bounds read in XI2 class parsing via size_classes() and copy_classes() (bsc#1281606).\n- CVE-2026-93543: out-of-bounds read in XI2 class parser (bsc#1281608).\n- CVE-2026-93544: out-of-bounds read in XI2 XIQueryDevice reply parsing (bsc#1281609).\n- CVE-2026-93545: out-of-bounds read in ListInputDevices() (bsc#1281612).\n- CVE-2026-94281: out-of-bounds read in XListInputDevices() class parsing (bsc#1281615).\n- CVE-2026-94282: out-of-bounds read in XI2 enter/leave/focus cookie conversio (bsc#1281651).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "openSUSE-Leap-16.0-1867",
        "title": "Patchnames"
